{
  "_readme": "Every application the desktop sidecar can open a directory in, and what each one IS. The id vocabulary crosses the language boundary: the Go sidecar's per-OS spec tables key their detection on it, and the browser keys its icon table on it, so the two were hand-written copies held together by a comment before this contract. `oses` states where a spec table must carry the id, which turns the old hand-written core-set test into a mechanical comparison. `kind` gives the app menu its grouping without testing an id literal anywhere; it maps to the ExternalAppKind proto enum, so a new kind fails generation until it lands here. Detection itself -- which binary, which bundle, which probe order -- stays Go-only under the one-side-only rule, and so do the display names, which the sidecar reports at runtime.",
  "kinds": {
    "EXTERNAL_APP_KIND_EDITOR": "a code editor or IDE the user installed",
    "EXTERNAL_APP_KIND_FILE_MANAGER": "the operating system's own file manager, always present"
  },
